{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bborbe/ai-assistant/pulls/106","id":4641271037,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTre2QM8AAAABFKQs_Q","html_url":"https://github.com/bborbe/ai-assistant/pull/106","diff_url":"https://github.com/bborbe/ai-assistant/pull/106.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/bborbe/ai-assistant/pull/106.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bborbe/ai-assistant/issues/106","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bborbe/ai-assistant/pulls/106/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bborbe/ai-assistant/pulls/106/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bborbe/ai-assistant/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bborbe/ai-assistant/issues/106/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bborbe/ai-assistant/statuses/370ce9ecaab65f7135e6f2f87c5342eb55376b55","number":106,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: optional /ben single-command mode via SLASH_COMMAND_MODE","user":{"login":"YetAnotherGerrit","id":97293098,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcyTKg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97293098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit","html_url":"https://github.com/YetAnotherGerrit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds `SLASH_COMMAND_MODE`, which selects the shape of the slash-command surface:\n\n- **`multi`** (default, legacy): unchanged. Every command is top-level and hidden behind `ManageGuild`. An existing deployment registers exactly what it did before, and a test pins this.\n- **`single`**: one `/ben` command carrying the same commands as subcommands (`/ben join`, `/ben status`, `/ben mode`, …), visible to every member of the guild. It takes up one entry in the picker instead of a dozen generic names that collide with other bots.\n\nDetails:\n\n- Both shapes are built from **one** list in `src/slash-commands.js`, so they can't end up offering different commands. A test asserts the names match.\n- **Authorisation is identical in both modes:** `config.isAllowed` and `config.isAdmin` run on every invocation, so in `single` mode a member outside `ADMIN_USER_IDS` sees `/ben` and is refused. The allowlist still fails closed.\n- `commandFor()` resolves the invoked command for the active mode. A command that arrives in the other mode's shape (still cached from the guild's previous list after a mode switch) gets an ephemeral pointer instead of being left hanging.\n- An unknown `SLASH_COMMAND_MODE` fails startup, so a typo can't silently register the wrong shape.\n- README env table, `local.env.example`, `src/config.js` comments and `CHANGELOG.md` (`## Unreleased`) updated.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `node --test`: 269/269 pass (run in a `node:22` container). The existing command-list tests run against both modes.\n- [x] `eslint .` and `prettier --check .` clean\n- [ ] `npm audit` / trivy (`make check`): not run\n- [ ] Real guild, `multi`: commands unchanged and hidden from non-`ManageGuild` members\n- [ ] Real guild, `single`: `/ben` visible to a non-admin member, refused with \"admin-only\"\n- [ ] Real voice session in `single`: `/ben join`, speak, confirm audio decodes; `/ben leave`\n\n---\n\n**Update 2026-10-02 — follow-up landed on top of this branch.**\n\nThe branch is merged up to `master` (`v0.56.0`), so it is no longer `CONFLICTING`. Three changes on top of the original:\n\n- The hard-coded `/ben` is now configurable per deployment: `SLASH_COMMAND_NAME` (default `ben`, validated as 1-32 characters of `[a-z0-9_-]`, refused at startup when invalid). Several assistant identities run from this one codebase, so without it any two of them in one guild register the same top-level name — the picker collision the single-command shape exists to avoid.\n- `single` mode preserves the public command tier `52743d1` introduced. The admin gate is applied to the **resolved subcommand**, not the wire name: `ADMIN_COMMANDS.has(i.commandName)` can never match inside the wrapper, so the original form would have re-gated every subcommand. `join`/`status`/`mode` stay open to any allowlisted member; `new`/`sessions`/`switch` stay admin-only.\n- A stale `slashCommandMode` comment claiming authorisation was \"identical in both\" modes corrected.\n\n`node --test`: 300/300 pass. `prettier --check` and `eslint` clean. The three live-guild checks above are still outstanding, and are what this branch needs before it is done.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-25T18:20:04Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T19:24:44Z","closed_at":"2026-10-02T19:24:44Z","merged_at":"2026-10-02T19:24:44Z","merge_commit_sha":"7e2cfd9f6afcf404e9132f22155fe0c2e3041dd4","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"YetAnotherGerrit:feat/ben-subcommands","ref":"feat/ben-subcommands","repo":{"id":1388019070,"node_id":"R_kgDOUrt9fg","name":"ai-assistant","full_name":"YetAnotherGerrit/ai-assistant","owner":{"login":"YetAnotherGerrit","id":97293098,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcyTKg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97293098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YetAnotherGerrit","html_url":"https://github.com/YetAnotherGerrit","followers_url":"htt